A||N||37||NIFE [PaulV]||Borla Exhaust||||1||
Z||000000||NIFE [PaulV]||10-08-2001||09:48 PM||||Am interested in hearing from anyone who has purchased and installed the Borla exhaust for the V6. Difficulty in mounting?, Tip alignment, performance improvement? Price paid with or without tips?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Rick 88||10-08-2001||11:49 PM||||A friend of mine put a Borla system on his 86 GT  4-speed along with a set of Jet hot coated Fiero Store headers.<P>The system looks very nice but it is too coarse sounding for my taste. The exhaust tips are smaller than the stock GT's so I would skip them. His tips are a little low in the opening but I think that was done during installation.<P>As for performance, It seems to feel faster but it is much louder under acceleration. I would not want to take a long trip in the car with the exhaust drone.<P>Rick <BR>yellow 88 GT 5-speed||||reg||1
Z||000002||Spiff||10-09-2001||12:45 AM||||Sorry I can't help because I am trying to find a Borla exhaust to buy. I have a Flowmaster on my Formula and it is very loud while driving on the highway. If you know of any Borla exhaust's for sale let me know.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||10-09-2001||01:18 AM||||Paul,<BR>Gargoyle (Dale) bought one and installed it. Installation was not bad, he had a shop do it. Tips cannot be adjusted It is all welded together.<BR>Sent you his Email address.<P>------------------<BR>             <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">           <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><B><I>Happiness isn't around the corner...<BR>Happiness IS the corner.</I></B></FONT><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 10-09-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Old Lar||10-09-2001||08:24 AM||||Paul, I had Bob Steiger (Twin Lakes Fiero)install Borla systems on my my two GTs. The 88 was more difficult than the 87 for the install or so I was told. (The Borla on the 88 seems to fit better) They sound great especially up around 4000 rpm.  I don't know much on performance improvement, but my gas milage is 30+ mpg for both cars over the road, including my 88 with a 3.4L and t 440 automatic.  Cruising at 2000 rpm, they aren't offensive sounding.<P>I got them with Borla tips for $495 each.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Alex4mula||10-09-2001||09:01 AM||||I installed one in my 88 3.4 Formula with no cat and FOCOA headers. Mine came without tips. Too small and old fashioned for my taste. It was installed at a muffler shop but it wasn't hard at all. Cut after cat, plug the pipes and weld if you want (at least after cat). Tips installation depends on the installer abilities. Mines came out perfect. The sound is just a little bit throatier than a stock muffler without cat. Not annoying at all. No resonation at all in my case. I don't consider it loud but definitely is not like stock. I found 88 Formulas to be very quiet. No one that has heard it has found it loud. A Flowmaster is loud. My gas mileage is near 30mpg in highway too. Go for it if you can find it. Good luck  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>    Alex4mula<BR>:) Red & White (:||||reg||1
Z||000006||Jefrysuko||10-09-2001||09:06 AM||||So Paul,<BR>You going to show us why it is you want to know these things or do we have to wait till after winter? <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT_4.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||NIFE [PaulV]||10-09-2001||09:30 AM||||The reason for asking is that the Borla system may again be available in the next 30 days. Tim Perrigo had them for sale, you could buy with tips or without. His site  (fieroparts.com) still has the info and pictures, but no longer shows any prices for either of the systems. I also recall some install problems, since the pipes did not have the brackets for the suspension springs. Still looking for the original prices....I see one response at $495.00 with tips.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Old Lar||10-11-2001||09:11 PM||||The Borla systems on my two cars.  Bob welded brackets on the 88's pipes to hang everything properly.  I haven't crawled under the 87 to see if he did the same, but I imagine he did. The same system hang differently on the two cars.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Side_3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
