Z||000012||AkursedX||10-12-2001||09:25 AM||||I'm interested in it too, keep us all updated on when it will be available.  I'll be wiating!!<P>------------------<BR><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic2_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000013||fieroparts.com||10-12-2001||11:03 AM||||You guys are all pissed that The Fiero Store<BR>copied Rodney Dickmans ideas, well we just found out that Twin  Lakes Fieros is having these made for them. We are the ones that spent<BR>1,000's of dollars (R & D)to get them made, now Bob<BR>is coping our system. Well, we have an exclusive with Borla, but I guess you can't trust anyone anymore?  We spend all the money to bring this system to market and now someone eles will make all the profits.<BR>????????????????? anything to make a buck!<BR>It's crap like this that makes me re-think<BR>why I got into the Fiero business 12 years ago?????????||||reg||1
Z||000014||1FST2M6||10-12-2001||11:03 AM||||when somone get one of these systems.. will they PLEASE dyno before and after... or contact me and i'll see if i can't get you a deal on dyno time for this test... ||||reg||1
Z||000015||Oreif||10-12-2001||02:51 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fieroparts.com:<BR><B>You guys are all pissed that The Fiero Store<BR>copied Rodney Dickmans ideas, well we just found out that Twin  Lakes Fieros is having these made for them. We are the ones that spent<BR>1,000's of dollars (R & D)to get them made, now Bob<BR>is coping our system. Well, we have an exclusive with Borla, but I guess you can't trust anyone anymore?  We spend all the money to bring this system to market and now someone eles will make all the profits.<BR>????????????????? anything to make a buck!<BR>It's crap like this that makes me re-think<BR>why I got into the Fiero business 12 years ago?????????</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>I thought you couldn't get them from Borla anymore. The copying of Rodney's stuff wasn't that Rodney used a supplier then the Fiero Store used the same supplier. The Fiero Store used Rodney's parts as a model and made their own to exactly match his. If Borla is still manufacturing them, They are not being "copyied" They are being sourced thru a different vendor. If you have an exclusive with Borla, then that is who you need to discuss this with. The customer pressure won't work. In the case of the Fiero Store we in effect boycotted their Store (which is the main souce of their income since it is all fiero parts) until they agreed to the popular opinion of not copying Rodney's part's. With Borla we cannot boycott them if they are not making anything at present.<BR> As an example of what I mean, Archie has parts for his V-8 kits made "exclusively for him" He drew up a legal contract for this. The supplier cannot sell any of Archie's parts to anyone without Archie's permission. If you have an agreement simular to this with Borla then you have a valid complaint.<P>If I remember you had a deal with Borla to make "X" amount of systems. Now that they are not available, and someone else is willing to also have Borla make "X" amount of systems, That is Borla's choice. <BR>Wouldn't be better to get in on the deal and have some more made? Then there would be two places someone could buy a Borla system. Also with 2 vendors selling your product, maybe Borla would't do a "limited run", the system would be readily available and the cost to make them would lower, then the  vendors can sell them for less. This would mean Borla and the vendors still have the same profit margine, But Borla's manufacturing costs would be less, The suppliers buy cost would be less, and the retail cost to us the consumers would be less. Sounds like a win-win situation to me.<BR>(Ooops the line about side scoops was in error, Sorry)<P> I would hate to lose ANY vendor of Fiero Parts since the availability of good parts is far and few.<P>------------------<BR>             <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">           <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><B><I>Happiness isn't around the corner...<BR>Happiness IS the corner.</I></B></FONT><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 10-12-2001).]||||reg||5
Z||000016||Slammed Fiero||10-12-2001||02:57 PM||||Former Fiero racer Andy Bettencourt had his stock exhaust Flow tested by Callaway, Without the cat in place it worked better than several aftermarket systems he had on the car (88 formula)<P>I have Borlas on the vette. Drone at highway speeds. Nice craftsmanship , but a ressonance at certian rpms that would make your ears bleed. (87 L98)<P>JM||||reg||1
Z||000017||Alex4mula||10-12-2001||03:03 PM||||That droning would be in a Vette. Too bad for it. My Fiero system is far from making your ears bleed and has no resonance. Let's compare apples to apples.<P>------------------<BR>    Alex4mula<BR>:) Red & White (:||||reg||1
Z||000018||fieroparts.com||10-12-2001||04:00 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Oreif:<BR><B> <BR>I thought you couldn't get them from Borla anymore. The copying of Rodney's stuff wasn't that Rodney used a supplier then the Fiero Store used the same supplier. The Fiero Store used Rodney's parts as a model and made their own to exactly match his. If Borla is still manufacturing them, They are not being "copyied" They are being sourced thru a different vendor. If you have an exclusive with Borla, then that is who you need to discuss this with. The customer pressure won't work. In the case of the Fiero Store we in effect boycotted their Store (which is the main souce of their income since it is all fiero parts) until they agreed to the popular opinion of not copying Rodney's part's. With Borla we cannot boycott them if they are not making anything at present.<BR> As an example of what I mean, Archie has parts for his V-8 kits made "exclusively for him" He drew up a legal contract for this. The supplier cannot sell any of Archie's parts to anyone without Archie's permission. If you have an agreement simular to this with Borla then you have a valid complaint.<P>If I remember you had a deal with Borla to make "X" amount of systems. Now that they are not available, and someone else is willing to also have Borla make "X" amount of systems, That is Borla's choice. <BR>Wouldn't be better to get in on the deal and have some more made? Then there would be two places someone could buy a Borla system. Also with 2 vendors selling your product, maybe Borla would't do a "limited run", the system would be readily available and the cost to make them would lower, then the  vendors can sell them for less. This would mean Borla and the vendors still have the same profit margine, But Borla's manufacturing costs would be less, The suppliers buy cost would be less, and the retail cost to us the consumers would be less. Sounds like a win-win situation to me.<P>You have some excellent product's available that I plan on purchasing next month for my "winter projects" (Already have the excellent side scoops.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  ) I would hate to lose ANY vendor of Fiero Parts since the availability of good parts is far and few.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>We do have a contract with Borla!  Now Borla told me that they will make the systems for Bob but will chang the tips to make it look<BR>like a diffent system.  It is just is not worth<BR>the BS<P>? we do not sell side scoops?<BR>I think you have us mixed up with<BR>the fiero store?<P>||||reg||14
Z||000019||Oreif||10-12-2001||06:33 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fieroparts.com:<BR><B> We do have a contract with Borla!  Now Borla told me that they will make the systems for Bob but will chang the tips to make it look<BR>like a diffent system.  It is just is not worth<BR>the BS<P><BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>OK my question would be, On your website, it states you have "sold out" all your sets and have "No plans to have anymore made".<BR>With the popularity of Fiero's here, and the reputation of Borla, Why are you opposed to not letting the rest of us have a Borla system on our cars? Since you state you have no plans to have more made, why get angry when someone else wants to have some made?<BR>Since you brought up Rodney before, Rodney makes parts and kits to replace items no longer available. It would seem to me that at present, Borla systems for the Fiero are no longer available. With the intrest in others wanting Borla systems, it would appear the demand for them is there.<P>I'm sorry if this offends you, but from my point of view, If you don't want to have more made, then I see no reason why someone else can do it. It is your choice to not have anymore made. The only way I can see this being advantagous is if you plan on increasing the value of your car by saying it has a "Rare" Borla system.<P>Borla is in the business of selling exhaust systems. If they see a "demand" they will sell the "supply". Especially if the tooling and specs for such a system are already set-up.<P>Why don't you want to have anymore made? There looks to be 4-5 potential customers in this thread alone. <P>Finally, What "design costs" did you have? Per your website, It uses a Borla designed muffler. The rest of the system is stainless steel pipes. <p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 10-12-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000020||btoth||10-12-2001||07:45 PM||||I know I would've bought a Borla system instead of the muffler that's laying under my bed, unlikely to be installed anytime soon, if someone had them available at the time I was looking.  <P>It's like K-Mart and Walmart... they carry the same stuff, it's all who's got what you need at the time that matters.||||reg||1
Z||000021||Fformula88||10-12-2001||09:04 PM||||I am going to have to side with Orief here a little bit.  If your not planning on having more exhausts made availble thru your operation, that shouldn't totally deprive anyone from getting one, or Borla from selling one.  <P>I can understand being upset if Borla is skirting your contract... but if you are no longer interested in buying exhausts from them I canunderstand their position too.  They don't make any money if they don't make/sell any exhausts and hence go out of business.  If it is a breach of contract, you should definately go after them.  Changing the tips certainly sounds like a weak enough reason to give them a terrible case!<P>I for one am very happy to hear they will be available again.  I was hoping to get one this spring when I heard they were sold out and would not be available again.  <P>I also want to take a moment to give a plug to Bob and Twin Lakes.  This guy has helped me find some stuff I couldn't on my own, has had the patience to let me chew his ear off at a FOCOA national for a while, and given me great prices to top it all off!  He certainly seems to be on the up and is a great source for the Fiero community IMO.    ||||reg||1
Z||000022||mrfiero||10-12-2001||11:04 PM||||I hate responding to these types of posts as I don't want to seem like a "mouthpiece" for any particular person or entity nor do I want to get in the middle of an argument.<P>However, we must remember that without Tim (Fiero Parts & Appraisals) there would not be a Fiero Borla system.  Borla would not have even built such a system if it weren't for Tim's insistence or perseverence.  I believe he shipped Borla a stock exhaust system overnight air (at his expense!) so the guys at Borla could start on a prototype.<P>He then solicited orders on this website (and others) and ordered then paid for these systems out of his own pocket.  It was only after he ordered them and paid for them that he requested payment from those who ordered one.  Many people backed out or never responded again, so he had to sit on several extra systems (above and beyond the extras he worked into the order).<P>I think what Tim is most upset about is the fact that someone else will be reaping the benefits of his work without any such effort on their part.  The longer an item is produced or the more of an item that is produced affects the cost of that item.  Initial costs are high due to the initial design work and costs of tooling up for production.  The cost to build an item decreases over time as more of that item are built.....this is the point where retail prices can be reduced without affecting anyones profit margin.  To my knowledge, Tim had beared this initial high cost and now someone else will benefit from the reduced costs.  Suppose person X will be able to sell Borlas for less than Tim did (because Borla will be able to charge less for them)......it will appear that Tim was overcharging for the systems before, even though that isn't true.  It is because person X did not have to incur the initial costs that he can sell at a lower price.<P>Let me clarify myself a little bit here.....I have no idea what Tim paid or what Bob will pay for the Borlas, but from an economic standpoint Bob will likely pay less overall for the systems he gets than Tim did.  So it is due to Tim's effort that Bob will be benefiting.<P>I also believe that Tim would have ordered up another batch if the need presented itself.  Remember though.....unless people pony up their $$$ upfront (before the systems are built) someone, be it Tim or Bob, will have to foot the bill and sit on their capital until all of the systems are sold.  Any potential profit then will not be realized until they are all sold, which makes it tough.  I know I wouldn't do it!<P>Botton line is that without Tim there would be no Fiero Borla system and if he had an exclusive deal with Borla then Borla should not try to weasel their way around it.  If there really were a ton of people lined up to buy the Borla system then why didn't these people contact Tim and persuade him to order up another run.  If no one calls how is he to know there is a demand?  Would these same people send their money in advance?  My guess is no.  They wouldn't want to tie up their $500 or so for potentially several months with the possibility that the systems could not be built (if there weren't enough orders to make a run).    <P>Also remember that Borla would never have made this system on their own accord.....the Fiero market is so small that they would not have given it a second thought (we're a pimple on the ass of the car market).<P>With that I will close.  I have no ill will towards anyone or their opinions on this matter and if Bob does in fact get in a shipment of Borlas then I wish him well.  I'm sure he will soon realize the frustrations of dealing with Fiero people who shop with their eyes but are afraid to open their wallets.  Everyone is always gung-ho about a project until it comes to fruition, then they disappear.  Ask Cliff about the archives on CD that everyone wanted (until he went out and made them). I'm sure he knows exactly what I am saying. <P>||||reg||1
Z||000023||Monkeyman||10-13-2001||10:04 AM||||So I guess the big question to fieroparts.com is this...Are you planning on selling any more Borla exhaust systems?  If you are, customers should probably go to you first (unless you are considerably higher than a competitor).  If not, what does all of this matter?<P>As far as ponying up 500 bills up front for what might be months, I wouldn't do it unless I know someone personally.  I understand that you spent a ton of money out of your own pocket.  That's admirable.  But...that's the cost of running a business.  Look at AusFiero for an example.  He's spent who knows how much money out of his own pocket.  And he's not had the opportunity to sell very much (damn fire).  Hopefully, he'll be able to sell lots of his Stage 2 kits and recoup his money plus a nice profit.  But if he doesn't, he's just out.<P>With that said, I hope you start to sell the Borla exhaust systems as well as Bob Steiger.  That way the price will be driven down and Borla might see that there is a continuing demand for these.  I don't need an exhaust system right now and even if I did, I couldn't afford 500 bucks.  When and if I need an new exhaust, I'll buy from whomever has the best price, service and reputation (BTW--simply having a good reputation isn't necessarily a deciding factor--the lack of a bad rep factors into it, too).||||reg||1
Z||000024||Fformula88||10-13-2001||10:15 AM||||I think I should clarify myself here...<P>I am in no way trying to flame anybody.  It was great for Tim to go thru the trouble to get the systems made and to market initially.  Like Rodeny, Bob, or any of the other Fiero people who have put considerable time, effort and mmoney into the Fiero market, Tim has made big contributions.  If you were offended by my previous post, I apologize.  <P>With that said... does anybody have any confirmation this is actually going to happen before we start a really big flame war??  PaulV, who are you expecting to have them back in stock?  Tim, have you talked to Borla yet?  I am sure you will, keep us posted on what you hear!!||||reg||1
Z||000025||fierosound||10-13-2001||01:09 PM||||I bought a BORLA system from Tim.  I felt the price was very fair.  Go to the BORLA site and you will see BORLA cat-back systems running up to and over $1000.  Almost none are as low priced as the systems Tim is selling for the Fiero.  The BORLA through Tim is also much less than "other"  SS systems for the Fiero.  To me, $150 for a muffler alone, plus installation costs on the old pipes, will put you half-way to a BORLA system anyway, so why not get the whole shebang, warrantied for 1 million miles??  The BORLA system is worth it, if you think your car is worth it.  Just had my car appraised and insured at $18,500 CDN, so it was worth it to me. I won't be replacing any exhaust parts ever again!<P> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/calgaryfieros/tonys87.htm" TARGET=_blank>www.geocities.com/calgaryfieros/tonys87.htm</A> <BR><p>[This message has been edited by fierosound (edited 10-13-2001).]||||reg||10
Z||000026||Dave Gunsul||10-13-2001||02:51 PM||||While it is true that Tim should be thanked<BR>for bringing the system to us, as Oreif already said, he has stopped selling them and<BR>has no interest in selling anymore. I emailed<BR>him when he first ran out of Borlas and asked him if he was going to make anymore and got absolutely no response at all.<BR>I guess the moral of the story is: if you drop the ball someone else will pick it up and run with it.<BR>From what I understand (talked to Paul last night on the phone) the Borla is a go and Bob<BR>should be selling it for less than Tim did but the final price has not been set on yet<BR>so don't quote me on that. Also: Bob is going to try out a couple of sets because the originals didn't have the exhaust springs<BR>brakets on them. He may offer them with the brakets already welded on the pipes to make instalation easyer. This too is not a done deal so don't start getting your hopes up to high. <BR>I want one no matter what i costs or comes with.<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver<p>[This message has been edited by Dave Gunsul (edited 10-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000027||danny boy||10-14-2001||12:48 AM||||AH-HA! So there IS a demand for SS Fiero exausts!!!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/PFF_sig_5.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000028||fierosound||10-14-2001||12:41 PM||||Danny...<P>There is ALWAYS a demand for BORLA exhaust when none are available.  BORLA didn't want to go through the bother of setting up all the jigs unless they are building  a minimum run of 50 units.  But as Tim found out, once they arrive and folks have to cough up their money to get one, the "interest" suddenly dwindles.  Tim's gone through this a couple of times. I'm not surprised that he is hesitant to get another order going. ||||reg||10
Z||000029||Fierowrecker||10-14-2001||01:28 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fierosound:<BR><B>Danny...<P>There is ALWAYS a demand for BORLA exhaust when none are available.  BORLA didn't want to go through the bother of setting up all the jigs unless they are building  a minimum run of 50 units.  But as Tim found out, once they arrive and folks have to cough up their money to get one, the "interest" suddenly dwindles.  Tim's gone through this a couple of times. I'm not surprised that he is hesitant to get another order going. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Perhaps most people are like me, if it is IN STOCK, I BUY, but if I have to wait for months and pay up front, forget it, I go elsewhere...<BR>What ever happened to the first stock of Borla exhausts? They got sold, right?<BR>It just took time to sell them, as the original exhaust system in a Fiero is stainless too!<BR>Basicly you end up paying for a name, the life expectancy, and perhaps a little performance gain over a Tuffy replacement exhaust system...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000030||Chris Schaefer||10-22-2001||06:42 PM||||So, is anything going to come from all of this?||||reg||5
Z||000031||NIFE [PaulV]||10-22-2001||07:13 PM||||The answer is YES, something will come out of this. Borla systems are on order, and will be available soon. They will be distributed by:<BR>Bob Steiger<BR>Twin Lakes Fiero<BR>Paxton, IL<BR>217-379-9140<P>The only question is final price, and the only reason to put that on hold is evaluating what needs to be done to properly attach the hangar brackets to the system so a DIY  install is possible. Plus, a test fit will be made on 88's and pre-88's so when received, everything will line up and install without any difficulty or additional parts purchases. This system will also work with 4 cylinders!!<BR>Bob will take reservations for these systems now, no down payment is necessary. No $$$ needed until ready to ship. Bob does take credit cards.||||reg||1
